<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Actuarial Valuation?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Estimating present value of future employee benefit payments using actuarial assumptions and PUCM. Each service year = additional benefit unit. DBO = present value of all accrued units at balance sheet date. Produces audit-ready report: DBO, plan assets, net liability, service cost, interest, gains/losses, sensitivity, disclosures. For <a href="/statutory-audit">Statutory Audit</a>, see our page.</p>
                    <p>For Gurugram companies: report contains everything the statutory auditor needs &ndash; DBO reconciliation (opening to closing), assumption justification, sensitivity analysis, and Ind AS 19/AS 15 compliant disclosures. For <a href="/private-limited-company-compliance">Pvt Ltd Compliance</a>, see our page.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Actuarial Valuation:</strong></p>
                    <ul><li><strong>DBO:</strong> Defined Benefit Obligation &ndash; present value of all projected future payments for past service</li><li><strong>PUCM:</strong> Projected Unit Credit Method &ndash; prescribed by Ind AS 19 and AS 15</li><li><strong>SSC 2020:</strong> 50% CTC wage rule + 1-year fixed-term. 25-50% DBO increase. Effective 21 Nov 2025</li><li><strong>Past Service Cost:</strong> DBO change from plan amendment. Immediately in P&amp;L (Ind AS 19)</li><li><strong>IALM 2012-14:</strong> Mortality table for Indian actuarial valuations</li><li><strong>Sensitivity:</strong> DBO impact of 0.5-1% assumption change. Required Ind AS 19 disclosure</li></ul>

                </div>
            </div>
